{% extends 'layouts/default-layout.twig' %}

{% set short_title = 'Documentation' %}

{% block content %}

<div class="h-entry">
    <h2 class="p-name"> {{ short_title }} </h2>

    <div class="e-content">
        <h3 id="micropub"> Micropub Requests </h3>
        <p> The <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/micropub/#json-syntax">Micropub JSON syntax</a> is used when indiebookclub posts to your endpoint. </p>

        <p> Example: </p>
        <pre>{
  "type": ["h-entry"],
  "properties": {
    "summary": ["Want to read: <b>Title</b> by <b>Author</b>, ISBN: <b>ISBN</b>"],
    "read-status": ["to-read"],
    "read-of": [
      {
        "type": ["h-cite"],
        "properties": {
          "name": ["<b>Title</b>"],
          "author": ["<b>Author</b>"],
          "uid": ["isbn:<b>ISBN</b>"],
          "photo": ["<b>Cover Image URL</b>"]
        }
      }
    ],
    "visibility": ["public"],
    "post-status": ["published"],
    "featured": ["<b>Cover Image URL</b>"]
  }
}</pre>

        <p> <code>read-status</code> will be “to-read”, “reading”, or “finished” based on your selection. </p>
        <p> <code>uid</code> will have a scheme of either <code>isbn:</code> or <code>doi:</code> based on your selection </p>
        <p> <code>author</code> and <code>uid</code> properties will only be included if you enter those fields. </p>
        <p> <code>visibility</code> will be “public”, “private”, or “unlisted” based on your selection. The private and unlisted options are only available if your Micropub endpoint indicates it supports them. </p>
        <p> <code>post-status</code> will be “published” or “draft” based on your selection. Note that drafts are only sent to your Micropub endpoint and are not stored on your indiebookclub profile. </p>
        <p> <code>featured</code>: If you use the <a href="{{ path_for('search') }}">book search</a> and Open Library has a cover image, this property will be the cover image URL. This URL is also sent in the <code>read-of.photo</code> property. Note: indiebookclub does not attempt to upload the image to your media endpoint. </p>

        <h3 id="query"> Query Parameters </h3>
        <p> The <a href="{{ path_for('new') }}">classic post</a> form accepts URL query parameters to pre-populate fields. This can be used with <a href="#bookmarklets">bookmarklets</a> to make adding new posts easier. </p>
        <p> <b>Parameters</b> </p>
        <p> Any combination of these parameters can be used. </p>
        <ul>
            <li> <code>read-status</code>: Values “to-read”, “reading”, or “finished” (not case-sensitive) </li>
            <li> <code>title</code> </li>
            <li> <code>authors</code> </li>
            <li> <code>isbn</code> </li>
            <li> <code>doi</code> </li>
            <li> <code>tags</code> </li>
            <li> <code>post-status</code>: Values “published” or “draft” (not case-sensitive) </li>
        </ul>

        <p> <b>Consuming read posts</b> </p>
        <p> You can provide a URL in the <code>read-of</code> parameter. If indiebookclub finds a <code>read-of</code> microformat at that URL, it will pre-populate the form with that information. If no <code>read-of</code> property is found, it will check for an <code>h-cite</code> microformat. </p>
        <p> Note that if the <code>read-of</code> query parameter is provided, it takes precedence over the other parameters listed above. </p>
    </div>

    <h3 id="bookmarklets"> Bookmarklets </h3>
    <p> Drag these links to your browser to make it easier to add posts. You can also use the source code in a <a href="https://caiorss.github.io/bookmarklet-maker/">bookmarklet editor</a> to customize them. </p>

    <p> <b><a href="javascript:(function()%7Blet%20%5Btitle%2C%20authors%5D%3Ddocument.querySelector('meta%5Bproperty%3D%22og%3Atitle%22%5D').attributes%5B'content'%5D.textContent.split('%20a%20book%20by%20')%3B%20let%20isbn%3Ddocument.querySelector('meta%5Bproperty%3D%22book%3Aisbn%22%5D').attributes%5B'content'%5D.textContent%3B%20let%20s%3Dnew%20URLSearchParams(%7Btitle%3A%20title%20%3F%3F%20''%2C%20authors%3A%20authors%20%3F%3F%20''%2C%20isbn%3A%20isbn%20%3F%3F%20''%7D)%3B%20window.location%3D'https%3A%2F%2F{{ getenv('IBC_HOSTNAME') }}%2Fnew%3F'%2Bs.toString()%3B%7D)()%3B">Add to indiebookclub from Bookshop.org</a></b> </p>

    <details>
        <summary>Javascript source:</summary>
        <pre>let [title, authors]=document.querySelector('meta[property="og:title"]').attributes['content'].textContent.split(' a book by '); let isbn=document.querySelector('meta[property="book:isbn"]').attributes['content'].textContent; let s=new URLSearchParams({title: title ?? '', authors: authors ?? '', isbn: isbn ?? ''}); window.location='https://{{ getenv('IBC_HOSTNAME') }}/new?'+s.toString();</pre>
    </details>

    <p> <b><a href="javascript:(function()%7Blet%20b%3DJSON.parse(document.querySelector('script%5Btype%3D%22application%2Fld%2Bjson%22%5D').textContent)%3B%0Alet%20s%3Dnew%20URLSearchParams(%7Btitle%3A%20b.name%2C%20isbn%3A%20b.isbn%2C%20authors%3A%20b.author%5B0%5D%5B'name'%5D%7D)%3B%0Awindow.location%3D'https%3A%2F%2F{{ getenv('IBC_HOSTNAME') }}%2Fnew%3F'%2Bs.toString()%3B%7D)()">Add to indiebookclub from Goodreads.com</a></b> </p>

    <details>
        <summary>Javascript source:</summary>
        <pre>let b=JSON.parse(document.querySelector('script[type="application/ld+json"]').textContent); let s=new URLSearchParams({title: b.name ?? '', isbn: b.isbn ?? '', authors: b.author[0]['name'] ?? ''}); window.location='https://{{ getenv('IBC_HOSTNAME') }}/new?'+s.toString();</pre>
    </details>

    <h3 id="export"> Export Posts </h3>
    <p> Your <a href="{{ path_for('settings') }}">settings</a> page has a button to download an HTML+<a href="https://microformats.org/">microformats</a> export of your posts. </p>
</div>

{% endblock %}

